60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate C, the Supplier Data Hub, would solve the misrouted deliveries and the copying of records.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, but would C create more work for the already exhausted coordination group or clerks?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Candidate A is out because of the network coverage. Candidate D sounds like it requires daily use by everyone, which Kenji said fails.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate B, the Training Studio, might be fixed-fee, but C fits the software allowance better if we manage the licenses.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with Shunichi. D is too broad. C is a specific tool for a specific problem, which usually survives.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, C consolidates records. It should reduce the clerical load of answering the same queries over and over.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"If it actually removes the need to hunt for data, I can support it.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"C is safer than A. A depends on customer site WiFi, which we know is unreliable.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,C is a software-based repository. It fits the available software allowance and avoids the frozen capital budget.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"C targets a specific inefficiency. It's not a ""daily entry for all"" tool, but a reference hub.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I really believe C is the most practical choice for the people on the floor.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,I'm convinced. Reducing the redundant queries is a win for the staff.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It's the most rational choice given the technical and financial constraints.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. It's affordable and doesn't risk a capital budget violation.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,It follows the pattern of the tools that actually survived in the past.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
